# Curl Cheat-Sheet

## Basic Downloads

### Download all sequentially numbered files (1-24)
```bash
curl [http://example.com/pic](http://example.com/pic)[1-24].jpg
```
*Uses globbing to fetch multiple numbered resources in a single command.*

### Save Output to a Specific File
```bash
curl -o filename.html [http://example.com](http://example.com)
```
*Saves the downloaded content to `filename.html`.*

### Save Output using Remote Filename
```bash
curl -O [http://example.com/file.zip](http://example.com/file.zip)
```
*Saves the file using its original name from the server.*

### Resume a Broken Download
```bash
curl -C - -O [http://example.com/largefile.zip](http://example.com/largefile.zip)
```
*Continues a previously interrupted download.*

