## Working with Headers & Metadata

### View Response Headers Only
```bash
curl -I [http://example.com](http://example.com)
```
*Fetches only the HTTP headers (HEAD request).*

### Include Headers in Output
```bash
curl -i [http://example.com](http://example.com)
```
*Displays both the response headers and the body content.*

### Pass a Custom Header
```bash
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN" [http://example.com/api](http://example.com/api)
```
*Sends a custom header, useful for API authentication.*

---

## Data Transfer & APIs

### Send a POST Request
```bash
curl -X POST -d "param1=value1&param2=value2" [http://example.com/resource](http://example.com/resource)
```
*Sends data to the server using the POST method.*

### Send JSON Data
```bash
curl -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"key":"value"}' [http://example.com/api](http://example.com/api)
```
*Sends a JSON payload with the appropriate content-type header.*

### Upload a File (Multipart/form-data)
```bash
curl -F "file=@/path/to/image.png" [http://example.com/upload](http://example.com/upload)
```
*Uploads a local file using a form POST.*

---

## Advanced Options

### Follow Redirects
```bash
curl -L [http://example.com](http://example.com)
```
*Automatically follows HTTP 3xx redirects to the final destination.*

### Use a Proxy
```bash
curl -x http://proxyserver:8080 [http://example.com](http://example.com)
```
*Routes the request through a specified proxy server.*

### Silent Mode
```bash
curl -s [http://example.com](http://example.com)
```
*Mutes the progress meter and error messages.*

---

## Option Reference Table

| Option | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| `-o` | Write output to a file |
| `-O` | Write output to a file named like the remote file |
| `-I` | Fetch HTTP headers only (HEAD) |
| `-L` | Follow redirects |
| `-H` | Custom header |
| `-X` | Specify request method (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE) |
| `-d` | HTTP POST data |
| `-u` | User credentials (user:password) |
| `-v` | Verbose mode (detailed connection info) |
| `-s` | Silent mode (no progress/errors) |

